From: Xaver Hugl <xaver.hugl@kde.org>
Date: Mon, 6 Oct 2026 14:20:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] inputmethod: immediately hide OSK when deactivating the input method
Description:
 This way, we don't need to wait for the roundtrip through the input method, and
 it avoids some intermediary resizes when the input method window stays open for
 longer than necessary.
 .
 Without it, a window that was shrunk for the on-screen keyboard keeps the
 reduced height when the application ends the text input by itself (e.g.
 Firefox when the user taps outside the text field): the keyboard goes away,
 the window stays small until it is activated again.
Origin: upstream, https://invent.kde.org/plasma/kwin/-/commit/0f3aee69d0b455d35064a20bc6ca983596f38407 (Plasma/6.7, in 6.7.6; master 10c89069e8f871b445fb4acb4c163095e2e4dec7)
Bug: https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=459136
License: GPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched file)
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
---
--- a/src/inputmethod.cpp
+++ b/src/inputmethod.cpp
@@ -257,6 +257,7 @@
     const bool wasActive = waylandServer()->inputMethod()->context();
     if (wasActive && !active) {
         waylandServer()->inputMethod()->sendDeactivate();
+        hide();
     }
 
     if (active) {
